r."},{"cn":"Greg Stewart","o":"Theatre Weekly","s":100,"b":"Rave","t":2,"u":"https://theatreweekly.com/review-mass-at-donmar-warehouse/","d":"2026-04-29","q":"<img decoding=\"async\" class=\"alignnone size-medium wp-image-1167\" title=\"Five Star Review from Theatre Weekly\" src=\"https://eghcszbxego.exactdn.com/wp-content/uploads/2015/10/New-5star-350x71.png?strip=all\" alt=\"Five Star Review from Theatre Weekly\" width=\"350\" height=\"71\" srcset=\"https://eghcszbxego.exactdn."},{"cn":"Unknown","o":"WhatsOnStage","s":100,"b":"Rave","t":2,"u":"https://www.whatsonstage.com/news/mass-stage-adaptation-at-donmar-warehouse-review_1719910/"},{"cn":"Stuart King","o":"London Box Office","s":89,"b":"Rave","t":2,"u":"https://www.londonboxoffice.co.uk/news/post/mass-donmar-review","d":"2026-05-02","q":"Under Carrie Cracknell's empathic direction... this is undoubtedly another triumph for the Donmar."},{"cn":"Demetrios Matheou","o":"The Arts Desk","s":80,"b":"Positive","t":2,"u":"http://theartsdesk.com/theatre/mass-donmar-warehouse-review-purgatorial-cat-and-mouse","q":"Cracknell, fresh from her triumph with Arcadia at the Old Vic, marshals all of this with economy and precision, deftly introducing some unexpected catharsis and a glimpse of value, in this bleak encounter, for the young lad watching from the wings."},{"cn":"The Reviews Hub - London","o":"The Reviews Hub","s":80,"b":"Positive","t":2,"u":"https://www.thereviewshub.com/mass-donmar-warehouse-london/","d":"2026-05-01","q":"At its best, Mass is a mesmerising fusion of incisive writing and extraordinary performances."},{"cn":"Holly O'Mahony","o":"London Theatre","s":76,"b":"Positive","t":2,"u":"https://www.londontheatre.co.uk/reviews/mass-review-donmar-warehouse","d":"2026-04-30","q":"It’s a masterful piece of writing from Kranz: every utterance counts, and each line is a turn of a cog that keeps this grim yet poignant narrative moving."},{"cn":"Unknown","o":"All That Dazzles  (UK)","s":100,"b":"Rave","t":3,"u":"http